   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 506 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the town of North Castle, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6713",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6713-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 506 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6713\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 506 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in the town of North\nCastle, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo extend by two years the authorization for the Town of North Castle to\nimpose a room occupancy tax not to exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1  extends  the Town of North Castle's room occupancy tax for\ntwo years until September 1, 2027.\n\n  Section 2 sets the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of North Castle seeks the continued authority to  impose  a  3%\ndaily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or similar place. This tax\nraises  revenues  to support municipal expenses. Chapter 506 of the Laws\nof 2016 granted the authority to the Town of  North  Castle;  this  bill\nwould  extend  the  expiration date for another two years from September\n2025 to September 2027.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S8040/A9612; L 2022, ch 416\n\n2019: S3708/A5269; L 2019, ch 204\n\n2016: S7134/A9691; L 2016, ch 506\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
